  <item>
    <title>Mapping in Drupal using OpenLayers</title>
    <link>http://2011.drupalcamp.es/node/247</link>
    <description>&lt;p&gt;Since the introduction of Google Maps, mapping has become a familiar task for most users. In this presentation, I&#039;ll show the state of art of mapping using the Drupal CMS and &lt;a href=&quot;http://drupal.org/project/openlayers&quot;&gt;OpenLayers&lt;/a&gt; module suite to create user-friendly and powerful maps in a very short timeframe. This approach to mapping in Drupal relies of familiar building blocks: CCK and Views, and their integration with OpenLayers using concepts such as behaviors, styles and layers. A basic understanding of Views and CCK is necessary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After this session, you will have a basic understanding of the state-of-the-art mapping tools for Drupal and how it can be practically implemented in your own site. The examples will be taken from a Drupal 6 installation, but most of this can be applied to Drupal 7 as well.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Slides from the presentation that has been given at the &lt;a href=&quot;http://drupal.cat/node/2011&quot;&gt;drupal.cat session&lt;/a&gt; can be found here: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.slideshare.net/pvhee/introduction-to-openlayers-in-drupal&quot; title=&quot;http://www.slideshare.net/pvhee/introduction-to-openlayers-in-drupal&quot;&gt;http://www.slideshare.net/pvhee/introduction-to-openlayers-in-drupal&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
