  <item>
    <title>Custom search forms with Apache Solr</title>
    <link>http://2011.drupalcamp.es/node/353</link>
    <description>&lt;p&gt;In this session we will work with Apache Solr from the code of a custom module. We will start installing Apache Solr and the &lt;a href=&quot;http://drupal.org/project/apachesolr&quot;&gt;apachesolr module&lt;/a&gt;. Then we will create a custom module with a search form with fields to filter, adding new fields to the Apache Solr schema, working a bit with the Solr query syntax and we will learn how to use some of the hooks and functions of the Apache Solr API.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This session is oriented to developers. We will be working with code during the major part of the session. So I recommend to have some experience working with Drupal modules and knowing a bit about what is Apache Solr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The sample module and a feature with the content type used can be found &lt;a href=&quot;http://valencia.drupal.es/sites/default/files/solr.tar.gz&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-type-userreference field-field-presenters&quot;&gt;
      &lt;div class=&quot;field-label&quot;&gt;Ponente(s):&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;field-item odd&quot;&gt;
                    &lt;a href=&quot;/users/david-hernandez&quot; title=&quot;Ver perfil de usuario.&quot;&gt;David Hernández&lt;/a&gt;        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;field field-type-filefield field-field-slides&quot;&gt;
